.TH CLIPSTACK 1 "November 2026" "clipstack 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipstack \- Win+V style clipboard history for Ubuntu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipstack
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipstack
records the text, links and images you copy and shows them in a small popup
when you press Super+B. Choosing an item puts it back on the clipboard and
pastes it into the window you were using.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR daemon " [" \-v ]
Watch the clipboard and record history. Started automatically at login.
The first time it runs for a user it adds the Super+B shortcut (once).
.TP
.B show
Open the history popup, or close it if it is already open.
.TP
.B clear
Delete all history items except pinned ones.
.TP
.B setup\-shortcut
Add the GNOME custom shortcut Super+B. Other shortcuts are not changed; if
Super+B is already used, it prints what uses it and changes nothing.
.TP
.B remove\-shortcut
Remove only the ClipStack shortcut.
.SH KEYS IN THE POPUP
Type to search, Up/Down to move, Enter to paste, Delete to remove an item,
P (or Ctrl+P) to pin or unpin, Esc to close.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clipstack/history.db
History database (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clipstack/images/
Copied images.
.TP
.I ~/.config/clipstack/config.json
Settings: max_items, auto_paste, paste_delay_ms, max_item_bytes, ignore_apps,
emoji_tab, popup_width, popup_height.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wl\-copy (1),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR xdotool (1),
.BR ydotool (1)
